---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PostList from '../components/PostList.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/display-picture.jpg';
import { SITE, getPosts } from '../site';

const posts = await getPosts();

const numbers = [
  { value: '8', label: 'engineers I led as tech lead: hiring, 1:1s, roadmap and on-call' },
  { value: '5+', label: 'client platforms I moved to Kubernetes and GitOps as the default' },
  { value: '30%+', label: 'lower infrastructure cost after moving to autoscaling Kubernetes' },
  { value: '10k+', label: 'learners on the Kubernetes platform I look after now' },
];

const cases = [
  {
    tag: 'Leadership',
    title: 'Leading a team of eight through a platform shift',
    summary:
      'As tech lead of eight engineers I hired, ran 1:1s and planned the roadmap with clients, while we moved more than five client platforms to Kubernetes and GitOps, with infrastructure changes reviewed like code.',
    href: '/work/#relayr',
    cta: 'More on my work page',
  },
  {
    tag: 'AI agents',
    title: 'How we let an AI agent work on our infrastructure safely',
    summary:
      'We wanted an AI agent to look into infrastructure problems without borrowing anyone’s access. So it got its own identity, short-lived credentials, a sandbox, and a hook that blocks anything we haven’t allowed.',
    href: '/2026-10-29/guardrails-for-ai-agents/',
    cta: 'Read the post',
  },
  {
    tag: 'Reliability',
    title: 'Why our load test kept failing at 170 users',
    summary:
      'A load test kept stalling at about 170 of 200 users, and every log looked fine. It took ten runs to find out that autoscaling was reconfiguring the load balancer in the middle of the test. Now all 200 get in.',
    href: '/2026-10-28/the-200-user-wall/',
    cta: 'Read the post',
  },
  {
    tag: 'Recovery',
    title: 'We had backups, but we’d never restored one',
    summary:
      'We had backups, but nobody had ever restored from one. I wrote the runbook and a script that works out which backups you need, and then we timed a real restore of the main databases.',
    href: '/2026-10-29/a-backup-counts-once-restored/',
    cta: 'Read the post',
  },
];
---

<Base>
  <section class="wrap hero">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <p class="eyebrow">Syed Usman · Engineering leader &amp; platform engineer · Berlin</p>
      <h1>{SITE.headline}</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Hi, I’m Syed. I spent two years as tech lead of eight engineers, and a decade building what teams run on:
        IoT products with their own hardware, client platforms on AWS and Azure, and the Kubernetes platform I look
        after now. For the past year almost all of my infrastructure work has gone through AI agents, and the part I
        care about most is the system around them: what they may touch, how their work gets reviewed, and how a team
        adopts them safely.
      </p>
      <p class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="/2026-11-08/how-i-use-ai/">How I work with AI</a>
        <a class="button button-quiet" href="/work/">See my work</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-portrait">
      <Image src={portrait} alt="Syed Usman, smiling, on a balcony above Berlin" width={480} height={600} fit="cover" position="top" loading="eager" />
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="ai">
    <div class="narrow prose home-ai">
      <h2 id="ai" class="section-label">How I work now</h2>
      <p>
        Anything I do more than a couple of times becomes a skill. For bigger projects we use a harness: sometimes
        the <a href="https://github.com/bmad-code-org/BMAD-METHOD">BMAD Method</a>, more often a simple one we built
        and tuned for our own team. Some of the best skills we use came from
        <a href="https://github.com/mattpocock/skills">Matt Pocock</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        One example I like: I have skills that learn the patterns in how my colleagues review code, the things they
        always comment on, and check my merge requests for them before anyone else sees them. The goal is a merge
        request nobody needs to leave a comment on.
      </p>
      <p>
        None of this replaces knowing the systems. That’s why the decade matters. I can tell when the agent is wrong,
        and I decide what it’s allowed to touch.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="numbers">
    <h2 id="numbers" class="section-label">A few numbers</h2>
    <ul class="numbers">
      {
        numbers.map((n) => (
          <li>
            <strong>{n.value}</strong>
            <span>{n.label}</span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="selected">
    <h2 id="selected" class="section-label">Selected work</h2>
    <div class="cases">
      {
        cases.map((c) => (
          <article class="case">
            <p class="case-tag">{c.tag}</p>
            <h3>{c.title}</h3>
            <p class="case-summary">{c.summary}</p>
            <a class="case-link" href={c.href}>
              {c.cta} <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </a>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="writing">
    <div class="narrow">
    <h2 id="writing" class="section-label">Writing</h2>
    <PostList posts={posts.slice(0, 5)} />
    {posts.length > 5 && <p><a class="case-link" href="/writing/">All writing →</a></p>}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="hello">
    <div class="narrow cta">
    <h2 id="hello">Working together</h2>
    <p>
      I’m always happy to hear about engineering management, staff, principal and lead engineering roles. I work from my own office near Berlin, and I’m there in person for onboarding, workshops
      and the moments that matter.
    </p>
    <ul class="facts">
      <li>Based in Berlin</li>
      <li>No visa sponsorship needed</li>
      <li>English (native), German (B1)</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="actions">
      <a class="button" href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
      <a class="button button-quiet" href="/syed-usman-cv.pdf">Download CV (PDF)</a>
    </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
